{
  "note": "The rest of the same 1901 enumerator's page as the Weinberg and Hunt households, transcribed from the image A. Hagues sent: schedules 132, 133, 134 and 136, and the cook at the top of the page who belongs to schedule 131, whose head is on the page before.\n\nOnly the Manns carry a house number. '5 North Road' is part of the record's 1 and 2 Albury Square / 3 and 5 North Road (#1), which holds no 1901 census, so they are filed there; Wright's Directory 1898-99 also prints '5 John L. Mann, of Mann & Co.' on North Road. The others give only a road, so they are added unfiled under the address the return gives:\n- 132, William Hickling, retired wine merchant, Duke William Mount. Wright's Directory 1894-95 and 1898-99 prints 'Mr. William Hickling' there without a number.\n- 133, William Small, hosiery manufacturer, Lincoln Circus. Wright's Directory prints William Small, of J. & R. Morley, and Miss Florence Small, artist, on Lincoln Circus in 1894-95 and 1898-99. He is already in the record as #2831, with notes only and no census, and is bound by number. The record also lists him as a resident of Flixton, 15 Cavendish Crescent North, which looks wrong and wants removing by hand. Miss F. Small (#2832) is not on this return.\n- 134, William Smith, lace manufacturer, at Claremont. The return writes 'Claremont Do' under Lincoln Circus, but Wright's Directory prints Claremont on North Road (George Sparrow in 1894-95, John Percy Smith in 1913-14), and the record has no house called Claremont, so it is left unfiled with both addresses stated.\n\nReadings to check against the image: Annie Smith's birthplace, written over (read here as Basford, Notts); Hannah Brown's age, 38 written over 34; Louisa Woolstenholmes's surname; Ellen Loach's surname. Ages are as the enumerator wrote them, so a birth year worked back from one may be a year out either way.",
  "source": "1901 census, Duke William Mount, Lincoln Circus and North Road, schedules 131 (part), 132, 133, 134 and 136, from the enumerator's page sent by A. Hagues. Directory evidence: Wright's Directory of Nottingham 1894-95, pages 59, 84 and 103 (Leicester Special Collections ids 164565, 164590, 164609); 1898-99, pages 65, 92 and 111 (ids 165241, 165268, 165287); 1913-14, page 165 (id 166521).",
